date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
abstract: "Local Operations Research Forum software and data snapshot supplied as Online Resource 2. Reuses the exact independently audited OMS v1.3.17 scientific-evidence archive, including generators, scaling software, saved runs, rational witnesses and license-free replay programs. Adds the ORF adaptation and a separate prospective within-family study of 24 generated scenarios, 360 primary MIP calls, a separate registered 360-call logging confirmation and 96 rational LP attempts with frozen policy settings and independent checks. Known parent data are reused; this is not external application validation. Accuracy-aware generation and verification lead the contribution; computational evaluation separates conditioning, solver effort, original-unit precision and full-process time. Performance remains instance- and configuration-dependent. A post hoc scenario-cluster bootstrap quantifies conditional uncertainty without treating seeds as independent problems; no clear incremental work or time advantage over L2 is established. The v1.6.0 update adds the closed 3,840-run confirmation and its full primary outcome, controls, strata and lossless raw archive. No general incremental time advantage over L2 is established. The v1.7.0 revision separately identifies post hoc written-bound acceptance sensitivity and retains the registered endpoint unchanged. The v1.7.1 packaging correction restores cluster installation helpers and the wheel lock without changing scientific data. The v1.7.2 editorial revision shares the full ClusterUY acknowledgement and consolidates repeated caveats without changing scientific results. The new Zenodo DOI remains deferred. Code is MIT; data/results are CC BY 4.0; manuscript text and PDFs are outside those licenses."
references:
